+# Tend UI Next Migration Candidate
+
+## Decision
+
+The next low-risk component is the global task search field. F-24 will migrate the existing native input to Tend UI `Input` through a second isolated adapter.
+
+F-23 selects and specifies the candidate only. It does not change the field or its behavior.
+
+## Why Input Is Next
+
+- the field has one stable location and one DOM identity: `#js-global-search`;
+- current behavior is narrow: trim the value, update `window.activeFilters.search` and invoke `window.applyFilters`;
+- Tend UI has a local `Input` source, public package export and Storybook stories;
+- the component forwards ordinary input props and supports a React ref;
+- migration can stay inside `src/integrations/tend-ui/` without moving filters or task state into React.
+
+## Contract To Preserve
+
+| Contract | Required F-24 result |
+| --- | --- |
+| DOM identity | The rendered native input remains discoverable as `#js-global-search`. |
+| Search behavior | Every input change updates `window.activeFilters.search` with a trimmed value. |
+| Filter refresh | Existing `window.applyFilters({ keepDrawerOpen: true })` behavior remains. |
+| Placeholder | `Поиск по задачам` remains visible. |
+| Layout | Search stays in the current toolbar position without shifting adjacent controls. |
+| Ownership | React owns only the search mount and existing Tend UI button mount. |
+| Regression | Card/table switching, filters and task rendering remain vanilla-owned. |
+
+## Intended Import
+
+```jsx
+import { Input } from '@10d/tend-ui/primitives/Input';
+```
+
+The adapter will be wrapped in the same `TendUI` provider contract used by the create-task button. Provider initialization should be shared before a second mount is introduced.
+
+## Verification Required In F-24
+
+- production build and all F-23 gates pass;
+- exactly one native input exists with `id="js-global-search"`;
+- typing a query filters the visible task set exactly as before;
+- clearing the query restores the previous result set;
+- layout and focus state are visually checked at desktop and mobile widths;
+- browser console contains no errors;
+- direct `dist/index.html` compatibility remains intact.
+
+## Rejected Candidates For This Step
+
+Table, Select, modal and column settings have broader state or interaction contracts. They remain later migration work after the second isolated primitive proves the adapter pattern.
